# Every path in this repository is owned by the project owner.
#
# Paired with the "review required (gate code)" branch ruleset (added
# 2026-10-27), which requires a pull request with an approving review from a
# code owner before anything lands on the default branch. This repository holds
# the estate's CI gate code (third-party/check.mjs and the allowlist), which every
# repo's workflows fetch, so a change here must be reviewable as a diff.
#
# Organization admins bypass in "pull request" mode only: they can merge their
# own pull request without a second approver, which avoids the solo-org review
# deadlock. They cannot push directly to main. Agents cannot approve on the
# owner's behalf.
#
# Consumers also pin this repository to a commit SHA with content hashes
# (.ai/tools/pin-github-checks.mjs in the Fancy envelope), so a merged change only
# reaches a repo when someone deliberately re-pins.
#
# The separate "main protection" ruleset blocks deletion and force-push.

